NOTE: this is the "durable hardening" change for the CI lint job. It targets
main as of a1af8e6, where the lint job still runs on Python 3.11. After PR #43
merges, that job runs on Python 3.15, so the `python-version: "3.11"` context
line below becomes "3.15" - apply with `git apply -3` or add the step by hand.

From aecc1cc2e1cdaece485bcdb2ca72a95a5abf1c07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:13:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): install build deps in lint job so lxml compiles when
 no wheel exists

The 'Lint & static checks' job installs the full requirements.txt but, unlike
the 'Python tests' job, never installed the C build dependencies. On Python
3.11 that was masked because lxml ships prebuilt cp311 wheels; on Python 3.15
no wheel is published yet, so pip falls back to compiling lxml from source and
fails with:

    Error: Please make sure the libxml2 and libxslt development packages are installed.

Mirror the python-tests job and install build-essential/pkg-config plus the
mysqlclient, libxml2/libxslt, libffi and openssl development headers before
installing the Python requirements, so the lint job no longer depends on a
wheel being published for the selected Python version.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 33d993d..24e4735 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -47,6 +47,11 @@ jobs:
         with:
           python-version: "3.11"
 
+      - name: Install system deps (mysqlclient + lxml builds)
+        run: |
+          sudo apt-get update
+          sudo apt-get install -y build-essential pkg-config default-libmysqlclient-dev libxml2-dev libxslt1-dev libffi-dev libssl-dev
+
       - name: Generate settings module
         run: cp frontend/frontend/settings.py.example frontend/frontend/settings.py
 
-- 
2.39.5

